Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:02.710 align:start position:0%
 
bro  i am rachel mckinsley  and i  take my eye out on the internet  i'm a retinoblastoma survivor  retinoblastoma  is cancer  in the retina of the eye and i lost my  eye at 18 months because by the time  they found  the tumor in the retina of my eye it was  too late to save the eye so i've grown  up just learning how to do everything  with one eye  because a child  is or a baby is very young they often  haven't learned to speak yet  and because the signs and symptoms are  very subtle  often a parent doesn't see anything  wrong it's not  a super  common  type of cancer but it is  the most common type of childhood care  to bring awareness they say  know the glow so when people take  pictures of their children or babies and  one eye reflects red eye and the other  reflects just white  it's because the flash is actually  reflecting off of the tumor in the eye  instead of off the retina which causes  the red i have a couple different  prosthetics my ocularist who is the  person that makes  my prosthetics is awesome  and i always wanted a gold eye and so  when i rocked up to her last time i was  in she's like girl yes  it's always apparent when somebody has a  prosthetic eye you can always tell a bit  there's there's always something that's  natural for humans to notice  something different  and so i wanted it to be a thing where  people knew that i was comfortable  enough to talk about it it wasn't until  i was a little bit older that i started  to get self-conscious about it and  that's why i created my instagram  account one-eyed and wonderful is to  find as many people that were struggling  with having an eye and be able to like  talk to them and shed some light and let  everyone know that they weren't alone so  many of my comments and everything are  like i have one eye too and i'm like  where are y'all at  when it's a slow day at the shop so you  take out your fake eye to scare your  employees  kate i got something for you  miranda  think fast  so every time i hear an eye pun i'm like  like there's a sick part of me that's  like  being able to find humor in any  situation  is going to make it better it just would  make everything more difficult if we  weren't  allowed to laugh about the things that  make us different i really hope that i  can just bring some awareness and also  put people who are in a similar  situation to myself at ease my favorite  thing is when i have parents  who  their child just lost an eye and they  are so  about what their future is going to look  like and  how they're going to cope with  everything as an adult like i just want  a lot of those parents to know that like  we grow up and we still  get to be awesome like it doesn't  doesn't change if anything it just makes  life a little more fun

